  "summary_en": "Opinion piece drawing on Levinas, embodied cognition and Stern to argue that anthropomorphic social-robot design optimizes functional social responsiveness, risking \"totalization\" that shapes expectations in human encounters and erodes ethical responsiveness to the Other. It rejects robot personhood and proposes a theoretical pathway.",
